# Hashin_unified

Concurrent topology and fibre-orientation optimisation of a composite plate: **minimise volume subject to a compliance limit and Hashin failure constraints**, 
with element density and fibre angle as design variables and MMA as the optimiser (MATLAB).

One code base, one optimiser (`main_heaviside.m`). The only thing that differs between the formulations being compared is the failure-constraint aggregation, 
selected with `opts.agg`:

| `opts.agg`    | Failure constraint                                                                                                            | Constraints returned |
|---------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---|
| `'separated'` | four Hashin mode indices (fibre tension, fibre compression, matrix tension, matrix compression), **each its own p-norm** over the elements       | 4 |
| `'smoothmax'` | Dong-type: fibre and matrix indices with Heaviside-blended allowables, combined by a **smooth maximum** at each Gauss point, then **one** p-norm | 1 |

Units are mm, N and MPa (compliance is in N·mm). A constraint value `g <= 0` is feasible; an index of 1 is failure.

## Quick start

Requires MATLAB R2022a or newer (`pagemtimes`, `decomposition`, `clim`). Run everything from this folder, because `Results/` and `Functions/` are found relative to it. 
Commit your changes before a run you want to keep (see *Results*).

```matlab
main_heaviside                                              % defaults: separated, P = 8, L-bracket
opts = struct('agg','smoothmax');          main_heaviside   % Dong-type baseline
opts = struct('p',16,'c_max',800);         main_heaviside   % any option from setOpts.m
clear opts                                                  % back to the defaults
```

`opts` stays in the workspace after a run, so the next run reuses it until you `clear opts`. Every run prints its options on the first line.

A short smoke test (coarse mesh, nothing saved, a few seconds):

```matlab
clear opts; opts = struct('ndiv',25,'maxiter',10,'win',5,'plot',false,'save',false); main_heaviside
```

Batch runs: `runCase` runs one options struct in its own workspace, so a loop's variables survive.

```matlab
addpath('Functions')
for P = [8 16 32]
    runCase(struct('agg','separated','p',P,'plot',false));
end
```

## Options

All options, defaults and validation are in `Functions/setOpts.m`. An unknown name is an error, and so is a value that is not implemented yet.

| Group   | Option      | Default     | Meaning                                                      |
|---------|-------------|-------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|
| problem | `problem`   | `'Lbrac60'` | `'Lbrac60'`, `'mbb'` or `'cantilever'` (see *Test problems*) |
|         | `ndiv`      | `100`       | elements along the 100 mm side (`Lbrac60` only)              |
|         | `rmin_phys` | `4`         | density and angle filter radius [mm]                         |
|         | `c_max`     | `250`       | compliance limit `F'*U` [N·mm]                               |
| material model | `penal` | `3`   | SIMP penalty               |
|                | `q`     | `0.8` | stress relaxation exponent |
| failure constraint | `agg`                   | `'separated'`     | `'separated'` or `'smoothmax'` |
|                    | `p`                     | `8`               | p-norm exponent **P on the linear stress-ratio index** (see below) |
|                    | `gate`, `k_gate`        | `'sigmoid'`, `50` | separated only: tension/compression gate and its sharpness [1/MPa] |
|                    | `eps_max`, `delta_frac` | `1e-3`, `0.05`    | smoothmax only: smooth-max regularisation; cubic-Heaviside half-width as a fraction of the smaller strength |
|                    | `eps_sq`                | `1e-12`           | keeps `sqrt(I)` differentiable at zero stress |
|                    | `pcorr`                 | `'off'`           | adaptive p-norm correction (not implemented yet) |
| filters, projection | `thetafilter` | `'double'` | pi-periodic double-angle filter (`'continuity'` not implemented yet) |
| | `eta`, `beta0`, `beta_max`, `beta_factor`, `beta_step` | `0.5`, `1`, `32`, `1.5`, `50` | Heaviside threshold; beta starts at `beta0` and is multiplied by `beta_factor` every `beta_step` iterations up to `beta_max` |
| optimiser | `maxiter` | `1000` | iteration limit |
| | `crow` | `[]` | scale of the compliance row for MMA. `[]` = automatic at iteration 1: `norm(df0dx)/norm(dc/c_max)` (about 229 for `c_max` 1941.74, 25.6 for 216.84) |
| | `fscale_coef` | `0.02` | objective scale `fscale = fscale_coef*numele` |
| | `theta_init`, `theta_pert`, `seed` | `pi/2`, `0`, `[]` | initial angle, seeded random perturbation of it (`+-theta_pert/2`, requires a `seed`), random seed |
| stopping | `win`, `tol_plateau`, `tol_g` | `20`, `1e-3`, `1e-2` | see *Stopping rule* |
| output | `plot`, `save` | `true`, `true` | figures; write the results file |

MMA constants (`raa0 = 0.01`, `move = 0.3`, `albefa = 0.1`, `asyinit = 0.5`, `asyincr = 1.2`, `asydecr = 0.7`) are in `Functions/mmasub.m`, one copy for every formulation. `c_MMA = 1e4`, `a0 = 1` are in `main_heaviside.m`.

## Formulation

**Problem.** Minimise the volume fraction `V/V0` (`V0` = area of the design domain) over element densities `x` in `[1e-4, 1]` and fibre angles `theta` in `[0, pi]`, subject to `c = F'u <= c_max` and `g <= 0`, with `K(x,theta) u = F`. The start is solid with `theta = pi/2`.

**Physical design.** Cone density filter of physical radius `rmin_phys`, then Heaviside projection (`eta`, with beta continuation). The angle is filtered through the double angle, `theta_phys = 0.5*atan2(H sin 2theta / Hs, H cos 2theta / Hs)`, so that `theta` and `theta + pi` average correctly. SIMP stiffness `x^penal` with a relative void-stiffness floor of `1e-9`; plane stress, orthotropic, 2 x 2 Gauss points per element.

**Stress.** Material-axis stress at each Gauss point, relaxed with the density: `sigma = x^q * C * epsilon`, giving `(s1, s2, t12)`. The strengths are `Xt, Xc` (fibre), `Yt, Yc` (transverse) and `S` (in-plane shear, also used as the transverse shear allowable). The element value of any index is its **area average over the four Gauss points**.

**`'separated'`** (`hashin_separated.m`). Gates `g1 = 1/(1+exp(-k_gate*s1))`, `g2 = 1/(1+exp(-k_gate*s2))`, quadratic indices

```
I_ft = (s1/Xt)^2 + (t12/S)^2        I_mt = (s2/Yt)^2 + (t12/S)^2
I_fc = (s1/Xc)^2 + (t12/S)^2        I_mc = (s2/Yc)^2 + (t12/S)^2
```

gated as `[g1*I_ft, (1-g1)*I_fc, g2*I_mt, (1-g2)*I_mc]`, stress-ratio index `FI = sqrt(I + eps_sq)`, and for each mode `k`:

```
g_k = ( sum_e FI_{e,k}^P )^(1/P) - 1  <=  0
```

**`'smoothmax'`** (`hashin_smoothmax.m`). Allowables blended by sign, `Hf = h(s1; Xt, Xc, delta_f)`, `Hm = h(s2; Yt, Yc, delta_m)`, with the cubic blend `h(c; a, b, d) = (a+b)/2 + 0.75(a-b)(c/d - c^3/(3 d^3))` for `|c| < d` (`a` above, `b` below), `delta_f = delta_frac*min(Xt,Xc)`, `delta_m = delta_frac*min(Yt,Yc)`. Then

```
FI_f = sqrt((s1/Hf)^2 + (t12/S)^2 + eps_sq)       FI_m = sqrt((s2/Hm)^2 + (t12/S)^2 + eps_sq)
H    = 0.5*[ (FI_f + FI_m) + sqrt((FI_f - FI_m)^2 + eps_max) - sqrt(eps_max) ]
g    = ( sum_e H_e^P )^(1/P) - 1  <=  0
```

Note the compression indices include the shear term, and the matrix-compression index is the simplified quadratic form, not the classical Hashin expression.

**What P means.** `P` is applied to the *linear* stress-ratio index `FI`. A p-norm of the quadratic index `I = FI^2` with exponent `p` is the same constraint as `P = 2p` on `FI`, so always quote `P`. The p-norm over-estimates the largest index (`max FI <= ||FI||_P <= N^(1/P) max FI`); a smaller `P` is more conservative.

**Sensitivities.** Adjoint, one right-hand side per failure constraint (4 for `'separated'`, 1 for `'smoothmax'`), solved with the factorisation of the stiffness matrix. Density sensitivities use `max(x, 1e-12)` in `x^(q-1)` and `penal/x`: once beta exceeds about 36 the projected density of void elements is exactly 0, and without the guard those entries are `NaN`.

## Stopping rule

After beta has reached `beta_max`, the run stops (`exitflag = 'converged'`) when both hold:

1. the volume fraction changed by less than `tol_plateau` (relative) over the last `win` iterations, and
2. `max([c/c_max - 1; g]) <= tol_g`.

Otherwise it runs to `maxiter` (`exitflag = 'maxiter'`). Greyness `M = 100*sum(4x(1-x))/numele` is logged but is **not** part of the rule, so check it. A run that ends on `maxiter` with the worst `g` oscillating just above `tol_g` is common; look at the end of `history` rather than the last iteration alone.

## Outputs

**Console.** One line per iteration: `C`, `obj(V)`, `M`, the constraint value(s), design change. The first line gives the options; with `crow = []` the automatic `crow` is printed at iteration 1. The final line gives `exitflag`, iterations, `V`, `c/c_max`, `max(g)` and `M`.

**Figures** (if `opts.plot`): 9 (design, every 5 iterations), 10 (fibre orientation), 11 (failure index per mode, or the single smooth-max index; 1 = failure), 12 (volume and constraints against iteration).

**Results file** (if `opts.save`): `Results/opt_results_<yyyymmdd_HHMMSS>_<agg>_P<p>_c<c_max>[_s<seed>]_<commit>[_dirty].mat`, saved with `-struct`, so `r = load(fullfile('Results', file))` gives:

| Field | Content |
|---|---|
| `xphy` | final physical design `[density; theta]` |
| `U`, `F`, `numele`, `numnode`, `coords`, `conn`, `edofMat`, `gs`, `freedofs`, `dphix_ref`, `dphiy_ref`, `matprop`, `strength`, `penal` | everything needed to recompute stresses from the saved design |
| `FailIdx` | element-averaged stress-ratio index: `numele x 4` (`separated`) or `numele x 1` (`smoothmax`) |
| `g_hs`, `vonMises`, `c`, `V`, `M`, `iter` | final constraint value(s), von Mises stress, compliance, volume fraction, greyness, iterations |
| `opts` | **every option of the run** |
| `exitflag` | `'converged'` or `'maxiter'` |
| `history` | `iterations x 10`: `[iter, c, V, change, g_ft, g_fc, g_mt, g_mc, M, seconds]` (for `smoothmax`, `g` is column 5 and columns 6-8 are `NaN`) |
| `commit`, `dirty`, `date`, `runtime` | git commit of the code, `1` if tracked files had uncommitted changes at the start, timestamp, wall-clock seconds |

A `_dirty` file cannot be reproduced from its commit hash: commit first. If every file shows `_dirty`, check `git config core.autocrlf`. Files you have not yet added to git are not counted.

To repeat a run: `git checkout <r.commit>`, then `opts = r.opts; main_heaviside`.

## Test problems

| `opts.problem` | Setup |
|---|---|
| `'Lbrac60'` | L-bracket, 100 x 100 mm outer, 40 mm legs (60 x 60 mm cut-out). Top edge of the vertical leg fixed. Downward load, total 200 N, spread over the top-edge nodes of the horizontal leg with `x > 95` (4 mm at the default mesh). The only problem used so far. |
| `'mbb'` | Half MBB beam, 100 x 50 mm, symmetry on the left edge, roller at the bottom-right corner, 400 N **point** load at the top-left corner. A point load is a stress singularity: stress-constrained results will depend on the mesh. |
| `'cantilever'` | 100 x 50 mm, clamped left edge, 400 N spread over five nodes at mid-height of the right edge. |

Material (all problems): `E1 = 39 GPa`, `E2 = 8.4 GPa`, `nu12 = 0.26`, `G12 = 4.2 GPa`; strengths `Xt = 1062`, `Xc = 610`, `Yt = 31`, `Yc = 118`, `S = 72` MPa. These are set in `main_heaviside.m`.

The older `problem_setup_Lbrac.m` (a bracket with 50 mm legs, filter radius in cells, different filter weights) cannot be selected and is not needed here; delete it if it was copied across.

## Verification and post-processing

**Finite-difference check.** `finitediff_main_heaviside.m` runs `main_heaviside` for a short run (edit its `opts` for the formulation), then perturbs the design variables and compares analytic and numeric sensitivities of `g` and of the compliance. It writes `finitediff_<agg>_P<p>.txt` and prints the relative L2 error per constraint, which is not distorted by the near-zero gradients of inactive modes. Run it once per formulation, and again after any change to a `Hashin` file.

**Tsai-Wu cross-check.** `[TW, g_tw, vonMises] = checkTsaiWu(file, doPlot)` recomputes the Tsai-Wu index of a saved design (no arguments: the newest file in `Results/`). It is a different criterion, not an accuracy check of the Hashin constraint.

**Demonstrations.** `demoAggregationOrder` (two elements, each critical in a different mode: stress at which each aggregation first reports `g = 0`, at the optimiser's `P` and over a sweep of `P`) and `demoModeConflict` (fibre against matrix tension at one material point). Both read their constants from `setOpts`.

**Reference numbers.** These two runs gave iteration histories identical to the two folders this one replaced (tested in Octave); in MATLAB they should reproduce the table to about six digits.

```matlab
clear opts; opts = struct('agg','separated','rmin_phys',4,'crow',230,'ndiv',25,'maxiter',10,'win',5,'plot',false,'save',false); main_heaviside
clear opts; opts = struct('agg','smoothmax','rmin_phys',5,'crow',230,'ndiv',25,'maxiter',10,'win',5,'plot',false,'save',false); main_heaviside
```

| Run | Iteration | C | obj(V) | g |
