## Status

- [x] Both aggregations reproduce the earlier folders (10 iterations, 25-division mesh, tested in Octave).
- [x] Finite-difference smoke test (6 iterations, 12 elements): per-constraint relative L2 error between 3e-8 and 5e-4 for both aggregations.
- [ ] Parity check repeated in MATLAB.
- [ ] Full finite-difference run, `separated`.
- [ ] Full finite-difference run, `smoothmax`.
- [ ] `mbb` and `cantilever` run with this code.

## Known limitations

- 2D plane stress, one load case, structured mesh only (the shape-function derivatives are precomputed once).
- The p-norm is conservative and the amount depends on `P` and on how many elements are near critical, so it also depends on the mesh. There is no adaptive correction yet.
- No minimum-length-scale control beyond the density filter and projection: one-element members can appear.
- The stress is the area-averaged index per element, so a Gauss-point value can exceed 1 while the element value is below it. Check designs with an independent, unaggregated evaluation.
- With the greyness limit removed from the stopping rule, a run can be "converged" and still grey; always check `M`.
- `ndiv` is supported for `Lbrac60` only.

## Not implemented yet

These are options in `setOpts.m`, but selecting anything other than the default raises an error:

- `gate = 'cubic'` (cubic smoothstep gate instead of the sigmoid),
- `pcorr` (adaptive p-norm correction),
- `thetafilter = 'continuity'` (fibre-continuity filter).

## Earlier folders

| Earlier folder | Equivalent run |
|---|---|
| `Hashin (weight minimised)` | `opts = struct('agg','smoothmax','rmin_phys',5)`, plus whatever `c_max`, `crow` and beta settings its `main_heaviside.m` had |
| `Mode-Seperated Hashin (weight minimised))` | `opts = struct('agg','separated','rmin_phys',4)`, likewise |
| `Hashin`, `Mode-Seperated Hashin` (compliance minimisation) | not supported; kept in `archive/` |

The earlier folders set `crow` by hand (230, 45, 25); the default here is automatic.

Example command: clear opts; opts = struct('problem', 'Lbrac60', 'agg','separated','rmin_phys',4,'ndiv',100,'maxiter',2000,'win',25,'plot',true,'save',false); main_heaviside

## Files

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `main_heaviside.m` | the optimiser (a script); options through `opts` |
| `finitediff_main_heaviside.m` | finite-difference check of the sensitivities |
| `Functions/setOpts.m` | every option, its default, and validation |
| `Functions/Hashin.m` | dispatcher on `opts.agg` |
| `Functions/hashin_separated.m`, `hashin_smoothmax.m` | the two failure-constraint formulations |
| `Functions/FE_analysis.m` | assembly and Cholesky factorisation |
| `Functions/objective_function.m`, `volume_constraint.m` | compliance and volume with sensitivities |
| `Functions/mmasub.m`, `subsolv.m` | MMA |
| `Functions/heavisideProjection.m`, `filterTheta.m`, `apply_filter_and_projection.m` | projection and filters (the last is used by the finite-difference script) |
| `Functions/problem_setup_Lbrac60.m`, `problem_setup_mbb.m`, `problem_setup_cantilever.m` | geometry, boundary conditions, load, filter matrix |
| `Functions/SF_FE.m`, `gauss_domain.m`, `nodes_in_support.m` | shape functions, quadrature, neighbour search |
| `Functions/saveOptResults.m`, `getGitInfo.m`, `runCase.m` | saving with provenance, git hash, batch helper |
| `Functions/checkTsaiWu.m` | Tsai-Wu post-check of a saved design |
| `Functions/demoAggregationOrder.m`, `demoModeConflict.m` | demonstrations |
| `Functions/TsaiWu.m`, `calculatePrincipalStress.m` | older helpers, not used by `main_heaviside` |
| `Results/` | created at run time; `.gitignore` excludes `Results/*.mat` |

## Troubleshooting

- `Unknown option "..."`: a typo in an option name; the message lists the valid names.
- `... is not available`: the value is not implemented yet (see above), or misspelt.
- `Undefined function 'runCase'`: run `addpath('Functions')` first.
- `Cholesky decomposition requires ...` in `FE_analysis`: usually a `NaN` in the design. Check that the `max(x,1e-12)` guards are in both `hashin_*.m` files.
- `Matrix is close to singular` from `subsolv`: warnings are no longer suppressed. Look at the constraint values and greyness in the log; a diverging run shows large `g` values first.

